WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.129
You know how when you hear that something
costs government $800 billion, it can be kind

00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:08.560
of hard to really make that number practical.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:13.050
It's such a big number, hard to make coherent
sort of practical sense of it.

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:19.220
And the same is true for the number of lies
that Donald Trump has told over 928 days in

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:27.720
office, which was as of August 5th about a
week ago, Donald Trump has told 12,019 lies.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.619
This is the latest tally from the Washington
Post's analysis.

00:00:30.619 --> 00:00:33.840
This is about 13 lies per day over the entire
presidency.

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:38.750
Now, as we've become accustomed to the Washington
Post doesn't want to call them lies, they

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.790
call them false or misleading claims.

00:00:40.790 --> 00:00:45.220
And I've talked a little bit about the possible
legal repercussions of actually using the

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:47.990
word lie, but they are lies.

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:50.460
And Donald Trump lately is lying even more.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:55.531
The average for the presidency is 13 lies
per day, but since April of this year, it's

00:00:55.531 --> 00:00:57.650
been 20 lies per day.

00:00:57.650 --> 00:01:00.390
As I earlier, the lies are often about immigration.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:04.890
They've also been about the economy, about
trade, about Russia.

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.860
And I do agree that this is a problem.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.940
Donald Trump either can't or won't tell the
truth, but for me the real issue is the sort

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:18.340
of quality and outrageous and audacious nature
of the lies rather than just the quantity

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:19.340
of lies.

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:24.179
The quantity is shocking, but Donald Trump
has basically skated free from his lies.

00:01:24.179 --> 00:01:30.320
And a big reason for that is that his followers
will rationalize the lies away with something

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:33.710
like, oh, all politicians lie.

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:38.859
But they believe that even though Donald Trump
lies, just like any other politician, Trump

00:01:38.859 --> 00:01:44.259
has the right ideas and he's doing the right
things, and it leads to zero accountability,

00:01:44.259 --> 00:01:47.000
no impact, no effect, no consequences.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:54.459
Now, I want to believe that independent and
centrist voters do care about the lying and

00:01:54.459 --> 00:01:58.659
that therefore, when we finally have a democratic
nominee, the Democratic nominee needs to be

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:04.280
equipped to call Trump out on the lies during
the general election debates or the Democratic

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.229
nominee is simply going to have no chance.

00:02:06.229 --> 00:02:12.340
I know that we've talked about cognitive decline
and that's a good conversation to have about

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:18.310
Trump, but there's actually a much more obvious
condition, a personality disorder, narcissistic

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:24.430
personality disorder, and this may make it
difficult for the eventual Democratic nominee

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:27.640
to really effectively call Trump out on his
lies.

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:33.189
At first, let's just look at the uh, criteria
for narcissistic personality disorder, which

00:02:33.189 --> 00:02:38.420
requires at least five of the following nine,
a grandiose sense of self importance.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:43.800
That's absolutely something Trump has a preoccupation
with fantasies of unlimited success, power,

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:46.260
brilliance, beauty or ideal love.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.090
Trump certainly has that.

00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:53.610
A belief that he or she is special and unique
and can only be understood by or should associate

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:57.329
with other special or high status people or
institutions.

00:02:57.329 --> 00:03:02.959
100% the need for excessive admiration, obviously,
I mean, it's almost like describing Trump,

00:03:02.959 --> 00:03:08.280
a sense of entitlement, of course, interpersonally,
exploitive behavior.

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:14.349
Yes, a lack of empathy, obviously envy of
others or a belief that others are envious

00:03:14.349 --> 00:03:15.860
of him or her.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:21.329
110% a demonstration of arrogant and haughty
behaviors or attitudes.

00:03:21.329 --> 00:03:28.299
Trump hits nine out of nine and only five
of these are required a criteria for a diagnosis

00:03:28.299 --> 00:03:30.450
of narcissistic personality disorder.

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:31.689
So this is what we have.

00:03:31.689 --> 00:03:36.319
It's pretty clear Trump, his entire life has
been of the mindset that he just needs to

00:03:36.319 --> 00:03:41.890
say whatever will get him through the next
30 seconds and it'll all get cleaned up later,

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:43.610
usually by somebody else.

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:48.280
So I think that the idea of just having a
democratic nominee that will call Trump out

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:53.109
about his lies during the debates is not going
to be as much of an easy win as some people

00:03:53.109 --> 00:03:54.190
might imagine.

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:58.420
Trump is good at one thing, which is surviving
the next 30 seconds.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:02.519
And if Donald Trump can survive the next 30
seconds and then the 30 seconds after that

00:04:02.519 --> 00:04:07.879
and then the 30 seconds after that during
the debate, uh, that may be enough to keep

00:04:07.879 --> 00:04:13.969
him from losing his supporters, his core supporters,
because he's able to just save face and get

00:04:13.969 --> 00:04:15.010
out of the debate.

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:16.359
When you're president.

00:04:16.359 --> 00:04:19.299
The lies are a major problem for the economy.

00:04:19.299 --> 00:04:22.430
They're a major problem for our relationships
with other countries.

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:26.710
But Donald Trump's approach is going to continue
to be the same and it is one of surviving

00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:32.080
the next 30 seconds, say whatever you can
to get through the next minute and then deal

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.870
with the repercussions on the back end often
with even more lies.

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:39.560
So this is something that is going to be an
issue during the debates.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:44.040
I think it's going to be more difficult than
some might imagine for the Democratic candidate

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.139
to actually hurt Trump with.

00:04:46.139 --> 00:04:52.090
And speaking of the general election debates,
will any network hosting the general debates

00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:58.720
have the testicular fortitude, for lack of
a better term, to call out Trump every time

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:03.599
that he lies and call out the Democratic candidate
for lies as well, by all means.

00:05:03.599 --> 00:05:10.560
But will they have the bravado and the strength
to face the critiques that they have it in

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:12.630
for Trump so to speak?

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.940
Or will they simply call out?

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:18.650
That is not true, Mr President, what you just
said is untrue.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:24.390
It's a an easy moral decision for me, but
I can bet you that the networks are going

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:28.210
to find it a much more difficult decision
to make and they probably will not call out

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:31.560
Donald Trump's lies during the general election
debates.

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:32.560
Let me know what you think.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.990
Makes sure you are following the David Pakman
show on

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:37.280
twitch at twitch.tv/david Pacman.

00:05:37.280 --> 00:05:40.992
I will be screaming at this evening at 6:30
PM eastern time and I hope you'll join me

00:05:40.992 --> 00:05:41.000
there.

